        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">

                <div class="heading mb-60">

                    <h3 class="heading__title text-center">Mobile Laser Clinic</h3>

                    <div class="about__Text">
                        <p class="mb-30">Skin City is committed to bringing world-class dermatology and laser technology
                            to every corner of Maharashtra and Karnataka. Unlike traditional clinics that focus only on
                            urban areas, Skin City extends its advanced treatments to rural communities, ensuring
                            accessibility for all.<br>

                            To bridge the gap in specialized dermatology care, Skin City operates a Mobile Laser Clinic,
                            offering dermatological and laser treatments on a fortnightly or monthly basis in districts
                            such as Aurangabad, Nanded, Jalna, Parbhani, Latur, Osmanabad, Bijapur, Gulbarga, Mumbai,
                            and Belapur. This initiative makes high-quality skin and hair treatments
                            available to people in remote areas, promoting inclusive dermatology care.
                        </p>


                    </div>


                </div>
                <!-- </div> -->
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row">

                <div class="heading mb-60">

                    <h3 class="heading__title text-center">Skin City CSR</h3>

                    <div class="about__Text">
                        <p class="mb-30">Janaki Medical and Social Foundation (JMF), the charity wing of Skin City,
                            provides expert dermatology care to underprivileged communities through concessional OPDs
                            and free skin camps in Solapur and Osmanabad districts. JMF actively works to raise
                            awareness about vitiligo, organizing forums, lectures, and awareness camps to eliminate
                            stigma. It also observes Vitiligo Day annually to educate the public. JMF co-funded the
                            Marathi film “Nital”, highlighting real-life challenges of vitiligo patients. Recognized for
                            its social contributions, JMF received the ‘Pride of India’ award, presented by Goa’s Chief
                            Minister, Digambar Kamat.
                        </p>


                    </div>


